                "quoted_status_profile_username": "foxnewspolitics",
                "reply_count": 13,
                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The Supreme Court got it right. Tennessee\u2019s law protects kids from being pushed into irreversible medical procedures before they\u2019re old enough to understand the consequences. That shouldn\u2019t be controversial. States have a duty to step in when activist agendas try to override common sense.\n\nThis is why I have a bill to ban gender experimentation on minors. Vulnerable kids are being deceived into surgeries or life-altering drugs they shouldn\u2019t even have to contemplate. Minors shouldn\u2019t be making permanent decisions to alter their bodies, and adults, especially in the medical field, have no business coercing them into it. Let kids be kids. This isn\u2019t compassionate care, it\u2019s irreversible harm.",
